1
00:00:00,833 --> 00:00:02,750
[zombie-like moaning]

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:04,083
[groaning and moaning]

3
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:06,958
[thumping head]

4
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:11,541
Any sign
of the illicit invaders?

5
00:00:11,541 --> 00:00:13,708
Not seeing a peep
with my peepers.

6
00:00:13,708 --> 00:00:14,833
[grumbling]

7
00:00:14,833 --> 00:00:16,250
I suppose that doesn't
make a difference,

8
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:18,416
considering we couldn't even
see the attackers

9
00:00:18,416 --> 00:00:19,791
when they were attacking us
last night.

10
00:00:19,791 --> 00:00:23,625
[scoffing] Invisibility
requires reams of permits

11
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:25,291
and background checks.

12
00:00:25,291 --> 00:00:27,916
Who could our assailants
have been?

13
00:00:27,916 --> 00:00:29,125
Who knows,

14
00:00:29,125 --> 00:00:31,750
but if they return,
they won't be invisible

15
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:34,666
to how hard I'm gonna
bludgeon them with fines.

16
00:00:34,666 --> 00:00:35,666
[panicking]
They can't come back.

17
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:38,208
I can't handle it
if they come back!

18
00:00:38,208 --> 00:00:40,416
What they did to Carl B,
and Debra,

19
00:00:40,416 --> 00:00:42,125
and the entire HR department!

20
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:44,416
Shh! Don't panic!

21
00:00:44,416 --> 00:00:47,750
Look at them, their minds,
their souls, are gone!

22
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:48,750
It can't happen to us,

23
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:50,375
I have so much to live for!

24
00:00:50,375 --> 00:00:52,333
Well, a few things
to live for.

25
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:54,041
I love my ergonomic chair.

26
00:00:54,041 --> 00:00:57,458
[unearthly note blowing]

27
00:00:57,458 --> 00:01:01,375
The unauthorized visitors
are back!

28
00:01:01,375 --> 00:01:03,458
[blowing unearthly note]

29
00:01:03,458 --> 00:01:05,458
Let's hit that scofflaw

30
00:01:05,458 --> 00:01:07,833
harder than I hit
the fourth floor vending machine

31
00:01:07,833 --> 00:01:09,458
when it doesn't release
my snacks!

32
00:01:09,458 --> 00:01:10,541
[weapon powering up]

33
00:01:10,541 --> 00:01:12,833
[agent yelping,
unearthly note blowing]

34
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:13,833
[screaming in terror]

35
00:01:13,833 --> 00:01:14,875
[groaning]

36
00:01:17,625 --> 00:01:19,708
[blowing unearthly note]

37
00:01:34,916 --> 00:01:38,416
[♪♪♪]

38
00:01:40,166 --> 00:01:44,625
[blowing unearthly note]

39
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:58,416
[ThunderFang]
The Source Dragons

40
00:01:58,416 --> 00:02:02,750
will rue the day
they rejected me.

41
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:06,458
[cackling wickedly]

42
00:02:08,291 --> 00:02:11,750
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

43
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:14,500
♪ Together we will rise ♪

44
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:17,958
♪ We fight ♪

45
00:02:17,958 --> 00:02:21,041
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

46
00:02:23,791 --> 00:02:25,416
[motors revving]

47
00:02:37,041 --> 00:02:39,583
The sun's setting already?

48
00:02:39,583 --> 00:02:41,750
Feels like the days
are getting shorter.

49
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:44,333
[Arin] Maybe it's
a magical Mysterium thing?

50
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:46,083
Ras, why are we stopping?

51
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:47,875
The dwellers of the Underworld

52
00:02:47,875 --> 00:02:50,333
do not appreciate
the presence of the living,

53
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:51,625
so entrances to their land

54
00:02:51,625 --> 00:02:54,708
don't remain in the same place
for long.

55
00:02:54,708 --> 00:02:56,375
I thought the Spectral Lands

56
00:02:56,375 --> 00:02:58,166
were where people passed through

57
00:02:58,166 --> 00:03:00,333
to whatever's after this life.

58
00:03:00,333 --> 00:03:03,166
So then, what's the Underworld?

59
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:04,291
[Ras] Similar,

60
00:03:04,291 --> 00:03:06,416
but only disgraced
warriors end up there,

61
00:03:06,416 --> 00:03:08,708
which is irrelevant
to our goals.

62
00:03:08,708 --> 00:03:12,791
All we need is access
to the Forge of the Forgotten.

63
00:03:12,791 --> 00:03:14,916
And this Forge will bring
my parents back?

64
00:03:14,916 --> 00:03:18,416
The Forge will enable us
to create a dragon icon

65
00:03:18,416 --> 00:03:20,458
to summon a Source Dragon,

66
00:03:20,458 --> 00:03:21,541
the first step to--

67
00:03:21,541 --> 00:03:23,166
Reversing the Merge, I know.

68
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:24,958
I just want to get to the part

69
00:03:24,958 --> 00:03:26,583
where you bring my parents back.

70
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:30,500
I have our heading.

71
00:03:31,916 --> 00:03:34,375
[engine revving]

72
00:03:35,958 --> 00:03:37,125
Enough, Sora!

73
00:03:37,125 --> 00:03:38,583
[sighing]

74
00:03:38,583 --> 00:03:39,833
You're no fun.

75
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:46,500
[revving]

76
00:03:50,458 --> 00:03:52,458
You shouldn't make him mad.

77
00:03:52,458 --> 00:03:53,583
I need him.

78
00:03:53,583 --> 00:03:55,041
He needs us, Arin.

79
00:03:55,041 --> 00:03:56,041
He wouldn't be dragging

80
00:03:56,041 --> 00:03:57,791
a couple of kid Ninja
around with him

81
00:03:57,791 --> 00:03:59,333
if he wasn't desperate for help.

82
00:03:59,333 --> 00:04:01,833
Just don't mess this up for me.

83
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:03,875
[revving motor]

84
00:04:12,291 --> 00:04:13,291
[Ras] We're here.

85
00:04:13,291 --> 00:04:15,250
Uh, you sure about that?

86
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,166
Yes, somewhere here

87
00:04:17,166 --> 00:04:20,416
is the passage
to the underworld.

88
00:04:22,541 --> 00:04:25,125
It's not even being guarded?

89
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:30,875
Okay, did we just see a mirage?

90
00:04:30,875 --> 00:04:33,208
I don't exactly know
how mirages work.

91
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:34,916
There has to be some way in.

92
00:04:34,916 --> 00:04:37,083
[heavy footsteps]

93
00:04:39,416 --> 00:04:41,333
[roaring]

94
00:04:41,333 --> 00:04:44,458
This thing doesn't look
happy to see us.

95
00:04:44,458 --> 00:04:46,625
Maybe we're falling
into a stereotype

96
00:04:46,625 --> 00:04:48,541
about scary skeleton monsters.

97
00:04:48,541 --> 00:04:49,875
It could be friendly.

98
00:04:49,875 --> 00:04:51,041
Excuse us!

99
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:53,625
We're just looking for
a way into the Under--

100
00:04:53,625 --> 00:04:55,208
Whaa--!

101
00:04:56,458 --> 00:04:57,875
[Jay] Ah, what a class!

102
00:04:57,875 --> 00:04:58,875
Who knew I could paint?

103
00:04:58,875 --> 00:05:00,333
I didn't know I could paint.

104
00:05:00,333 --> 00:05:01,708
I told you you could.

105
00:05:01,708 --> 00:05:03,791
You have a lot of skills,
actually,

106
00:05:03,791 --> 00:05:05,916
because you used to be a Ninja.

107
00:05:05,916 --> 00:05:08,000
Ugh, not this again.

108
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,916
Just when I thought
you were kind of fun.

109
00:05:09,916 --> 00:05:10,916
"Kind of"?

110
00:05:10,916 --> 00:05:12,791
Oh, I am a lot of fun.

111
00:05:12,791 --> 00:05:14,750
You've become the fuddy-duddy.

112
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:15,916
"Fuddy-duddy"?

113
00:05:15,916 --> 00:05:17,000
Did you learn that word

114
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,208
from our dance lessons
with the retirees?

115
00:05:19,208 --> 00:05:20,250
Maybe.

116
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:22,166
Those lessons
were the bee's knees.

117
00:05:24,375 --> 00:05:26,291
[calling] Lloyd!

118
00:05:26,291 --> 00:05:27,666
Wyldfyre?

119
00:05:27,666 --> 00:05:29,833
You mean Doyll and Filedwire!

120
00:05:29,833 --> 00:05:30,875
Right.

121
00:05:30,875 --> 00:05:31,958
We're home!

122
00:05:31,958 --> 00:05:32,958
Hmm.

123
00:05:32,958 --> 00:05:35,208
They should have been
back by now.

124
00:05:35,208 --> 00:05:37,708
Hopefully they found a lead
on Arin's parents.

125
00:05:37,708 --> 00:05:39,000
Hopefully,

126
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,541
but the Land of Lee
does have a lot of distractions.

127
00:05:42,541 --> 00:05:43,583
Let's look for them,

128
00:05:43,583 --> 00:05:44,750
just to make sure Wyldfyre

129
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:47,500
isn't eating
the ice cream hotel.

130
00:05:57,750 --> 00:06:01,208
It's no use
trying to escape that cage.

131
00:06:01,208 --> 00:06:05,541
It's designed to optimize
your journey to friendship.

132
00:06:05,541 --> 00:06:06,875
Just like Elway here,

133
00:06:06,875 --> 00:06:10,208
steadily having all the negative
thought-pollution about me

134
00:06:10,208 --> 00:06:11,791
cleaned from his mind.

135
00:06:11,791 --> 00:06:14,416
The things I'll do
for my friends, really.

136
00:06:14,416 --> 00:06:15,791
[Lloyd] I knew you had
to have brainwashed

137
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:17,125
everyone down here, Lee!

138
00:06:17,125 --> 00:06:18,125
What?

139
00:06:18,125 --> 00:06:20,250
Of course I didn't do that!

140
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:24,041
Everyone in the Land of Lee
has chosen to be here!

141
00:06:25,083 --> 00:06:28,166
Well, almost everyone.

142
00:06:28,166 --> 00:06:30,041
Once in a long while,

143
00:06:30,041 --> 00:06:32,500
some no-goodnik figures out

144
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:35,125
the "truths" I sing
about the Merge

145
00:06:35,125 --> 00:06:38,083
are not based in actual fact,

146
00:06:38,083 --> 00:06:41,291
and so those few have to be...

147
00:06:41,291 --> 00:06:42,791
corrected.

148
00:06:46,208 --> 00:06:47,375
[cage buzzing open]

149
00:06:47,375 --> 00:06:49,125
Hello, Elway!

150
00:06:49,125 --> 00:06:51,666
Hope you enjoyed
your meditation!

151
00:06:51,666 --> 00:06:52,750
Just wondering,

152
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:56,041
what do you think
about your old pal, Lee?

153
00:06:56,041 --> 00:06:58,416
Lee is a loyal, kind,

154
00:06:58,416 --> 00:07:02,000
and completely
non-deceptive friend.

155
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,333
Don't worry,

156
00:07:04,333 --> 00:07:07,458
when my little tentacled buddy
gets rested up,

157
00:07:07,458 --> 00:07:10,916
you two will be next to learn
the magic of friendship.

158
00:07:14,583 --> 00:07:15,750
[shouting in frustration]

159
00:07:18,625 --> 00:07:20,750
Heat is better than green.

160
00:07:20,750 --> 00:07:22,958
[grunting with effort] H'yah!

161
00:07:22,958 --> 00:07:24,333
That doesn't seem right.

162
00:07:24,333 --> 00:07:26,125
What can this cage
be made out of?

163
00:07:26,125 --> 00:07:28,583
Oh, no, not now...

164
00:07:28,583 --> 00:07:29,666
[vision whooshing]

165
00:07:29,666 --> 00:07:30,708
[Strength symbol]
We cannot get involved

166
00:07:30,708 --> 00:07:32,208
with mortal problems.

167
00:07:32,208 --> 00:07:35,375
It only poisons us
and our powers.

168
00:07:35,375 --> 00:07:36,833
Weakens us!

169
00:07:36,833 --> 00:07:38,125
[Motion symbol]
Like it or not,

170
00:07:38,125 --> 00:07:41,541
ThunderFang is a threat
to the Source Dragons.

171
00:07:41,541 --> 00:07:43,333
[Life symbol] Only because
we got involved with mortals

172
00:07:43,333 --> 00:07:44,750
in the first place.

173
00:07:44,750 --> 00:07:46,541
We should never
have made that promise

174
00:07:46,541 --> 00:07:48,208
to the First Spinjitzu Master.

175
00:07:48,208 --> 00:07:51,416
[Strength] I voted against
granting boons to the First,

176
00:07:51,416 --> 00:07:53,041
if you remember.

177
00:07:53,041 --> 00:07:55,250
[Motion] We all recall
it was a split

178
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:58,625
until the Source Dragon
of Balance favored the mortals

179
00:07:58,625 --> 00:08:01,625
and became the deciding vote,

180
00:08:01,625 --> 00:08:04,166
but Balance
is no longer with us,

181
00:08:04,166 --> 00:08:08,583
and we must reach a consensus
on our own.

182
00:08:08,583 --> 00:08:11,375
The only way
to truly defeat ThunderFang

183
00:08:11,375 --> 00:08:14,375
is through
the Arc Dragon of Focus.

184
00:08:14,375 --> 00:08:15,416
[Focus] No.

185
00:08:15,416 --> 00:08:17,708
I will not aid this time.

186
00:08:17,708 --> 00:08:20,250
[Energy] If it is so voted,
you shall,

187
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:22,208
like the last time.

188
00:08:22,208 --> 00:08:26,166
[Focus] I also regret
getting involved with mortals.

189
00:08:26,166 --> 00:08:29,583
It has brought us nothing
but pain and danger.

190
00:08:29,583 --> 00:08:33,125
We should remove
our presence entirely.

191
00:08:33,125 --> 00:08:35,041
[Motion]
It's too late for that.

192
00:08:35,041 --> 00:08:38,333
ThunderFang has more power
than you realize.

193
00:08:38,333 --> 00:08:40,916
He will force his way
onto this council

194
00:08:40,916 --> 00:08:43,000
and destroy everything.

195
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,625
[Focus] My answer is still no.

196
00:08:45,625 --> 00:08:46,916
[Motion] You do realize

197
00:08:46,916 --> 00:08:51,750
that a mortal could activate
the Arc Dragon of Focus.

198
00:08:51,750 --> 00:08:53,166
[Strength] Impossible!

199
00:08:53,166 --> 00:08:55,500
[Motion] If both halves
of the dragon

200
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,583
were released from their sleep

201
00:08:57,583 --> 00:08:59,666
and focused upon soul energy...

202
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:02,291
[Strength sniffing]
Is there a mortal here now?

203
00:09:03,458 --> 00:09:06,666
[gasping]

204
00:09:06,666 --> 00:09:08,416
How could you take a nap
at a time like this?

205
00:09:08,416 --> 00:09:10,916
Some leader.

206
00:09:10,916 --> 00:09:13,083
The Source Dragons...

207
00:09:13,083 --> 00:09:15,000
ThunderFang is back.

208
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,125
[gasping]

209
00:09:17,250 --> 00:09:20,916
Something tells me
they don't want us here, Ras!

210
00:09:20,916 --> 00:09:21,958
[Ras grunting with effort]

211
00:09:23,625 --> 00:09:24,583
[roaring]

212
00:09:24,583 --> 00:09:25,750
Aah!

213
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:28,375
[Kai] All right, Frak,
you got this.

214
00:09:28,375 --> 00:09:31,041
Remember,
half the battle is up here.

215
00:09:31,041 --> 00:09:32,541
You want me
to head-butt the bamboo?

216
00:09:32,541 --> 00:09:33,666
What? No!

217
00:09:33,666 --> 00:09:35,125
Just hit them normal,

218
00:09:35,125 --> 00:09:36,916
but with mental focus.

219
00:09:36,916 --> 00:09:38,250
Begin!

220
00:09:38,250 --> 00:09:39,625
H'ah! H'yah!

221
00:09:39,625 --> 00:09:40,750
H'yah!

222
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:41,750
[panting]

223
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:42,875
How was that?

224
00:09:42,875 --> 00:09:44,000
You're really improving.

225
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,500
[Geo] Refreshments!

226
00:09:47,041 --> 00:09:48,958
Thanks, Geo.

227
00:09:48,958 --> 00:09:50,875
Can you fuse that bamboo
so we can do another run?

228
00:09:50,875 --> 00:09:52,166
You bet.

229
00:09:52,166 --> 00:09:56,041
Tea, two sugars,
two more sugars, and honey,

230
00:09:56,041 --> 00:09:57,833
just the way you like it.

231
00:09:57,833 --> 00:09:58,916
[gasping] How'd you know?

232
00:09:58,916 --> 00:10:00,416
Hey, who made snacks?

233
00:10:00,416 --> 00:10:02,333
-[Geo] I did!
-[gagging]

234
00:10:02,333 --> 00:10:05,541
Sponge Wafers
with a hint of mint.

235
00:10:05,541 --> 00:10:06,958
Personal recipe.

236
00:10:06,958 --> 00:10:09,583
[wheezing] This just sucked
all the moisture out of my body.

237
00:10:09,583 --> 00:10:11,416
[gulping tea]

238
00:10:11,416 --> 00:10:12,666
[Fritz] Kai! Kai!

239
00:10:12,666 --> 00:10:14,958
Check out what we scavenged
from the geyser last week!

240
00:10:14,958 --> 00:10:16,458
[hoarsely] Can't wait.

241
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:20,583
Cool weapons, right?

242
00:10:22,041 --> 00:10:24,708
[coughing]
The Prismatic Blades?

243
00:10:24,708 --> 00:10:27,208
They went missing
when we fought ThunderFang.

244
00:10:27,208 --> 00:10:29,000
No one knew where they went,

245
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,333
so how'd they wind up
in the Land of Lost--

246
00:10:31,333 --> 00:10:33,250
Oh, yeah, I hear it now.

247
00:10:33,250 --> 00:10:35,166
Frak, this time,

248
00:10:35,166 --> 00:10:37,208
I want you to use
your elemental quake power

249
00:10:37,208 --> 00:10:40,416
to shatter the targets
from below.

250
00:10:40,416 --> 00:10:43,041
[ground rumbling]

251
00:10:43,041 --> 00:10:44,416
[yelping]

252
00:10:44,416 --> 00:10:46,541
It's like
the Earth is screaming!

253
00:10:46,541 --> 00:10:47,958
You can feel it too?

254
00:10:47,958 --> 00:10:50,208
I sense it everywhere
in the Merged Lands,

255
00:10:50,208 --> 00:10:52,375
but it's especially loud here.

256
00:10:52,375 --> 00:10:54,291
What's causing it?

257
00:10:54,291 --> 00:10:55,291
Not sure.

258
00:10:55,291 --> 00:10:57,083
All I know is a while back,

259
00:10:57,083 --> 00:10:59,000
the ghostly voice of Master Wu

260
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,041
called me on a mission.

261
00:11:01,625 --> 00:11:03,166
<i>[Master Wu] Cole...</i>

262
00:11:03,166 --> 00:11:05,000
Huh?

263
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:10,166
<i>[Cole] After walking</i>
<i>for what seemed like forever,</i>

264
00:11:10,166 --> 00:11:11,791
<i>I found the place</i>
<i>that must be the source</i>

265
00:11:11,791 --> 00:11:13,666
<i>of the screaming Earth.</i>

266
00:11:15,375 --> 00:11:17,541
<i>I could sense something</i>
<i>deep under ground,</i>

267
00:11:17,541 --> 00:11:19,208
<i>something big.</i>

268
00:11:19,208 --> 00:11:20,750
[ground rumbling]

269
00:11:20,750 --> 00:11:21,916
<i>I tried and tried,</i>

270
00:11:21,916 --> 00:11:23,875
<i>but couldn't get the object up.</i>

271
00:11:23,875 --> 00:11:25,333
<i>Why would Wu send me out there</i>

272
00:11:25,333 --> 00:11:27,208
<i>if I couldn't do</i>
<i>anything about it?</i>

273
00:11:27,208 --> 00:11:28,958
<i>Unless he wanted me to do more,</i>

274
00:11:28,958 --> 00:11:31,041
<i>and I just failed him</i>
<i>or something?</i>

275
00:11:31,041 --> 00:11:32,041
Whoa.

276
00:11:32,041 --> 00:11:34,125
What could be down there?

277
00:11:34,125 --> 00:11:35,916
Let's check it out right now!

278
00:11:35,916 --> 00:11:37,625
That sounds like a whole...

279
00:11:37,625 --> 00:11:39,791
ugh, what's the word
for it? "Journey."

280
00:11:39,791 --> 00:11:42,375
I for one am not in the mood
to go walking forever.

281
00:11:42,375 --> 00:11:43,916
I have something
that might help.

282
00:11:44,583 --> 00:11:45,458
[whooshing]

283
00:11:47,166 --> 00:11:50,458
[♪♪♪]

284
00:11:52,708 --> 00:11:54,083
You made this?

285
00:11:55,083 --> 00:11:56,750
Just fused together
a bunch of parts

286
00:11:56,750 --> 00:11:58,875
that wound up
in the Land of Lost Things.

287
00:11:58,875 --> 00:12:00,333
No big deal.

288
00:12:00,333 --> 00:12:02,416
You could give Sora
a run for her money.

289
00:12:03,541 --> 00:12:06,333
Okay, a journey it is.

290
00:12:06,333 --> 00:12:08,083
Yes!

291
00:12:08,083 --> 00:12:09,333
[grunting with impact]

292
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:13,208
Arin! No!

293
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:16,833
Yaah!

294
00:12:16,833 --> 00:12:18,458
Sora!

295
00:12:18,458 --> 00:12:19,708
You just did Spinjitzu!

296
00:12:19,708 --> 00:12:20,708
Did I?

297
00:12:20,708 --> 00:12:22,541
I did, right? Right?

298
00:12:22,541 --> 00:12:23,541
[rumbling]

299
00:12:23,541 --> 00:12:24,541
[roaring]

300
00:12:28,416 --> 00:12:29,291
Hup!

301
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:31,791
[roaring battle cry]

302
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:35,750
[roaring]

303
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:37,708
[gasping]

304
00:12:40,416 --> 00:12:42,083
[roaring]

305
00:12:42,083 --> 00:12:43,541
<i>Mortals!</i>

306
00:12:43,541 --> 00:12:45,333
<i>You gained victory</i>

307
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:46,875
<i>through the only thing</i>

308
00:12:46,875 --> 00:12:49,083
<i>the dishonorable warriors</i>
<i>of the underworld</i>

309
00:12:49,083 --> 00:12:51,458
<i>have ever respected--</i>

310
00:12:51,458 --> 00:12:52,958
<i>strength!</i>

311
00:12:52,958 --> 00:12:56,125
<i>Your passage has been granted.</i>

312
00:12:58,833 --> 00:13:01,041
Bone stairs into darkness...

313
00:13:01,041 --> 00:13:02,041
Cool.

314
00:13:02,041 --> 00:13:04,125
Love hanging out with you guys.

315
00:13:04,125 --> 00:13:05,416
[Ras] Move.

316
00:13:11,375 --> 00:13:12,625
[whistling nonchalantly]

317
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:13,875
Hey, Lee.

318
00:13:28,208 --> 00:13:30,250
Well, definitely following us.

319
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:32,958
Who's the paranoid egotist now?

320
00:13:32,958 --> 00:13:34,291
Both things can be true.

321
00:13:34,291 --> 00:13:35,583
Come on.

322
00:13:35,583 --> 00:13:37,541
[beeping]

323
00:13:37,541 --> 00:13:39,458
So this "backstage" area

324
00:13:39,458 --> 00:13:40,708
is supposed to be
a Lee-only zone?

325
00:13:40,708 --> 00:13:41,916
Mm-hmm.

326
00:13:41,916 --> 00:13:44,500
That's what Ellen Q
said at needlepoint class.

327
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:45,708
She also told me

328
00:13:45,708 --> 00:13:48,125
she sneaks extra cherries
at the ice cream social,

329
00:13:48,125 --> 00:13:49,416
but that sounded like
her problem.

330
00:13:50,541 --> 00:13:52,000
[lock beeping open]

331
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Got it.

332
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,083
Pretty good for someone

333
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:55,583
who claims to have
never been a ninja.

334
00:13:55,583 --> 00:13:57,833
Maybe I was just a good thief.

335
00:14:14,041 --> 00:14:15,541
Wish I had one of these.

336
00:14:15,541 --> 00:14:16,583
[kicking]

337
00:14:16,583 --> 00:14:19,083
In fact,
I deserve a little treat.

338
00:14:19,083 --> 00:14:21,291
What did you just do?

339
00:14:21,291 --> 00:14:22,291
You'll find out.

340
00:14:31,375 --> 00:14:32,708
[chiseling]

341
00:14:34,166 --> 00:14:36,208
Carving gravestones?

342
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:37,458
Read the names.

343
00:14:37,458 --> 00:14:39,000
Strong McCoolguy.

344
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,875
Nya McCoolguy.

345
00:14:40,875 --> 00:14:42,333
Dyoll Donmagar.

346
00:14:42,333 --> 00:14:44,583
Filedwire Donmagar!

347
00:14:44,583 --> 00:14:46,500
They're making
gravestones for us?

348
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:48,750
[chuckling]

349
00:14:48,750 --> 00:14:50,833
Time to roll the bones!

350
00:14:52,166 --> 00:14:55,333
You got a spare-- rib!

351
00:14:55,333 --> 00:14:56,791
[laughing]

352
00:14:56,791 --> 00:14:57,791
[Ras] You two!

353
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:01,625
Direct me to
the Forge of the Forgotten!

354
00:15:01,625 --> 00:15:02,666
Sure.

355
00:15:02,666 --> 00:15:03,791
Second left past the--

356
00:15:03,791 --> 00:15:05,208
You dummy,

357
00:15:05,208 --> 00:15:07,208
why you tellin'
some random mortal

358
00:15:07,208 --> 00:15:08,791
where the Forge is?

359
00:15:08,791 --> 00:15:11,583
Ah! He asked all forceful.

360
00:15:11,583 --> 00:15:13,958
You know I respond
to strong leadership.

361
00:15:13,958 --> 00:15:15,375
You bonehead!

362
00:15:15,375 --> 00:15:18,125
Look, mortal,
we'll only tell you

363
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:21,625
if you can beat us
at a bone-rolling challenge.

364
00:15:21,625 --> 00:15:23,125
Winner gets--

365
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:27,000
Okay, you win.

366
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,625
Ah! Second left
past the demon tree.

367
00:15:29,625 --> 00:15:31,291
Third passage.
You can't miss it!

368
00:15:33,083 --> 00:15:34,541
Sorry about him.

369
00:15:34,541 --> 00:15:36,875
He can get a little intense.

370
00:15:38,541 --> 00:15:39,875
Here you go.

371
00:15:39,875 --> 00:15:41,333
Yeah, we know the deal.

372
00:15:41,333 --> 00:15:42,875
We've worked with
people like that.

373
00:15:47,416 --> 00:15:49,125
Guess that's it.

374
00:15:49,125 --> 00:15:50,625
How do we work it?

375
00:15:58,208 --> 00:15:59,416
[gasping]

376
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,458
It's not responding
to my powers.

377
00:16:01,458 --> 00:16:04,583
Must be magic,
'cause it's not tech.

378
00:16:04,583 --> 00:16:06,750
[Ras] It is far
beyond technology.

379
00:16:07,916 --> 00:16:08,750
[pulling lever]

380
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:11,000
[deep rumbling and hissing]

381
00:16:15,083 --> 00:16:17,250
It's big enough to crawl into.

382
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:18,750
The Forge is powered

383
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:21,125
when someone enters
the Casket of Bones.

384
00:16:21,125 --> 00:16:22,208
Creepy.

385
00:16:22,208 --> 00:16:24,083
How do they get back out?

386
00:16:24,083 --> 00:16:25,083
They don't.

387
00:16:25,083 --> 00:16:26,416
Huh?

388
00:16:26,416 --> 00:16:30,416
Why do you think I tolerated
your presence for so long?

389
00:16:30,416 --> 00:16:32,125
I thought you needed my help.

390
00:16:32,125 --> 00:16:33,333
That's true,

391
00:16:33,333 --> 00:16:35,000
in a way.

392
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:37,500
No.

393
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:39,125
I won't let you do this.

394
00:16:39,125 --> 00:16:41,791
Rather it was you, Arin?

395
00:16:42,791 --> 00:16:45,250
No one dies here today, Ras!

396
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:46,791
Using this Forge

397
00:16:46,791 --> 00:16:49,541
is the only way
to save your parents.

398
00:16:49,541 --> 00:16:52,833
Someone is going
into that casket.

399
00:16:52,833 --> 00:16:54,000
You...

400
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,458
or her?

401
00:16:56,458 --> 00:16:59,500
Have I ever steered you wrong?

402
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:01,666
You were a weakling
when I found you,

403
00:17:01,666 --> 00:17:04,291
and I turned you into a warrior.

404
00:17:04,291 --> 00:17:07,791
Warriors must make
difficult choices,

405
00:17:07,791 --> 00:17:12,250
especially if they truly love
their parents.

406
00:17:15,958 --> 00:17:17,416
[quietly] Be stealthy.

407
00:17:20,958 --> 00:17:22,083
[headstones tumbling heavily]

408
00:17:24,250 --> 00:17:25,250
Uh...

409
00:17:25,250 --> 00:17:27,250
[quietly] Stealthy starting now!

410
00:17:39,041 --> 00:17:42,583
Pretty surreal to be looking
at your own grave marker.

411
00:17:42,583 --> 00:17:44,916
Does this mean
Lee's planning to kill us?

412
00:17:44,916 --> 00:17:46,416
It doesn't make any sense.

413
00:17:46,416 --> 00:17:47,666
[gasping] Look!

414
00:17:50,375 --> 00:17:51,750
Arin's parents?

415
00:17:51,750 --> 00:17:53,833
They really are dead.

416
00:17:53,833 --> 00:17:56,750
You were wrong, Jay.

417
00:17:56,750 --> 00:17:58,291
Look here.

418
00:17:58,291 --> 00:17:59,291
Melba.

419
00:17:59,291 --> 00:18:01,500
We met her yesterday
at dance class.

420
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:05,083
She's old, but definitely
not in that grave.

421
00:18:05,083 --> 00:18:07,583
I've got a hunch.

422
00:18:10,875 --> 00:18:11,958
It's empty!

423
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:14,291
I bet all these graves
are empty!

424
00:18:14,291 --> 00:18:15,333
But why?

425
00:18:15,333 --> 00:18:17,958
What if Lee puts these here

426
00:18:17,958 --> 00:18:21,333
to stop anyone who comes looking
for lost loved ones?

427
00:18:21,333 --> 00:18:23,375
They'd think the person
they're looking for is dead

428
00:18:23,375 --> 00:18:24,541
and give up.

429
00:18:24,541 --> 00:18:25,958
That way, no one would ever find

430
00:18:25,958 --> 00:18:28,041
his hidden
underground community.

431
00:18:28,041 --> 00:18:29,500
[Lee] Hey!

432
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:31,750
Who's lightninging
my cemetery?

433
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:34,458
Count and Countess McCoolguy?

434
00:18:34,458 --> 00:18:35,750
Stop!

435
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:39,208
[Arin] This wasn't
part of the deal, Ras.

436
00:18:39,208 --> 00:18:42,083
I never told you
our mission would be easy.

437
00:18:42,083 --> 00:18:45,625
You have never been closer
to bringing your parents back.

438
00:18:45,625 --> 00:18:47,166
Show me you have the courage

439
00:18:47,166 --> 00:18:50,666
to do what needs to be done.

440
00:18:50,666 --> 00:18:52,625
It's not fair.

441
00:18:52,625 --> 00:18:56,416
Have the strength
to save your family.

442
00:18:57,458 --> 00:19:00,750
Sora is my family too.

443
00:19:00,750 --> 00:19:03,208
You are defying me?

444
00:19:03,208 --> 00:19:06,250
I should have never trusted you
in the first place.

445
00:19:08,833 --> 00:19:10,416
So be it.

446
00:19:10,416 --> 00:19:11,416
[roaring]

447
00:19:17,791 --> 00:19:19,000
[Arin screaming]

448
00:19:21,041 --> 00:19:22,333
[Ras grunting]

449
00:19:29,291 --> 00:19:30,416
[roaring in rage]

450
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,750
H'ah!

451
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:34,833
[both screaming]

452
00:19:36,375 --> 00:19:39,208
[Arin and Sora screaming]

453
00:19:39,208 --> 00:19:40,500
[groaning]

454
00:19:42,958 --> 00:19:44,833
[roaring]

455
00:19:51,875 --> 00:19:54,750
You will enter that casket.

456
00:19:54,750 --> 00:19:56,958
You can't win, Ras,

457
00:19:56,958 --> 00:19:59,125
'cause we have
one thing you don't.

458
00:20:00,125 --> 00:20:01,125
[Arin] Each other!

459
00:20:02,583 --> 00:20:04,000
[grunting with effort]

460
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,125
Your loyalty to each other

461
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:09,791
will be your downfall!

462
00:20:11,583 --> 00:20:13,416
[slamming, rock crumbling]

463
00:20:13,416 --> 00:20:14,375
[crying out]

464
00:20:14,375 --> 00:20:16,666
[grunting with effort]

465
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:19,500
[heavy slamming]

466
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:21,333
[impact echoing]

467
00:20:23,916 --> 00:20:25,458
[grunting with effort]

468
00:20:27,208 --> 00:20:30,750
Let's go
before he digs himself out.

469
00:20:33,916 --> 00:20:35,500
[exhaling deeply]

470
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:38,083
Nothing beats the fresh air
of the living world.

471
00:20:38,083 --> 00:20:39,291
They're gone.

472
00:20:39,291 --> 00:20:41,166
They're gone forever.

473
00:20:41,166 --> 00:20:42,166
[sobbing gasp]

474
00:20:45,333 --> 00:20:47,166
[sobbing quietly]

475
00:20:51,125 --> 00:20:54,083
You once told me
change can be scary.

476
00:20:54,083 --> 00:20:56,166
I'm scared, Sora.

477
00:21:02,875 --> 00:21:05,041
[♪♪♪]

478
00:21:11,166 --> 00:21:12,458
Now that Lee's onto us,

479
00:21:12,458 --> 00:21:14,958
we need to find
Lloyd and Wyldfyre, and--

480
00:21:16,125 --> 00:21:17,875
I'm guessing Lee can still live

481
00:21:17,875 --> 00:21:20,041
even with a few less
of his bodies.

482
00:21:20,041 --> 00:21:21,833
Let's find out.

483
00:21:21,833 --> 00:21:23,208
Jay, we can't kill him.

484
00:21:23,208 --> 00:21:24,916
It's not the Ninja way.

485
00:21:24,916 --> 00:21:27,500
I'm not a Ninja!

486
00:21:33,541 --> 00:21:34,583
H'yah!

487
00:21:34,583 --> 00:21:36,166
[woman gasping]

488
00:21:36,166 --> 00:21:37,708
That was Spinjitzu.

489
00:21:37,708 --> 00:21:39,583
You're the Ninja!

490
00:21:39,583 --> 00:21:43,500
Our son, Arin,
was your biggest fan.

491
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:44,958
[gasping]

492
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

